 charge the year before. Free cash flow fell 32.5% to $8.7B, and Qualcomm returned $11.7B through buybacks and dividends."],"highlights":["Automotive chip revenue reached a record $6.0B, up 51.7%.","Licensing (QTL) kept a 72% EBT margin on $5.6B of revenue.","Diluted share count fell 2.9% to 1,073M.","Shareholders' equity rose 43.4% to $30.4B."],"watch":["Handset chip revenue fell 13.4%, and Q1 FY2027 revenue is guided to $10.4B–$11.2B.","Operating margin dropped to 20.1% from 27.9%.","Net income was driven by tax swings, not operations.","Net debt rose to $7.4B as cash and securities fell 24.4%."],"table":[["Revenues",43.12,44.284,1],["Cost of revenues",20.222,19.738],["Gross profit",22.898,24.546,1],["Operating expenses",14.24,12.191],["Operating income",8.658,12.355,1],["Investment & other, net",0.756,0.308],["Income before taxes",9.414,12.663],["Income tax (benefit)",-4.214,7.122],["Net income",13.628,5.541,1],["Diluted EPS ($)",12.7,5.01,0,"eps"],["Operating cash flow",11.145,14.012],["Free cash flow",8.651,12.82,1]],"sources":[["Qualcomm FY2026 Q4 earnings release","https://s204.q4cdn.com/645488518/files/content_files/FY2026-4th-Quarter-Earnings-Release.pdf"]]},"video":{"revenueLine":{"cap":"Handsets fell 13.4% to $24.1B while automotive grew 51.7% to $6.0B.","say":"Handset chip revenue fell 13.4 percent to 24.1 billion dollars, while automotive grew 51.7 percent to 6 billion."},"spotlights":[{"kicker":"Diversification","big":"$6.0B","sub":"automotive revenue · +51.7% YoY","lines":["IoT $7.1B, +7.8%","Handsets $24.1B, −13.4%"],"cap":"Automotive revenue grew 51.7% to a record $6.0B as handsets declined.","say":"Automotive revenue grew 51.7 percent to a record 6 billion dollars, offsetting part of the decline in handsets."},{"kicker":"Tax swing","big":"$13.6B","sub":"net income · 2.5× last year","lines":["$4.2B tax benefit in FY2026","Operating income fell 29.9%"],"cap":"Net income rose to $13.6B on a $4.2B tax benefit, though operating income fell 29.9%.","say"